      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the average value of the numbers \\(0\\), \\(2z\\), \\(4z\\), \\(8z\\), and \\(16z\\), we start by calculating the sum of these numbers and then dividing by the number of terms.\n\n1. **Calculate the sum of the numbers:**\n   \\[\n   0 + 2z + 4z + 8z + 16z\n   \\]\n   Group the terms to factor out the common factor \\(z\\):\n   \\[\n   0 + z(2 + 4 + 8 + 16)\n   \\]\n   Simplify the expression inside the parentheses:\n   \\[\n   0 + z(2 + 4 + 8 + 16) = 0 + z(30) = 30z\n   \\]\n   So, the sum of the numbers is \\(30z\\).\n\n2. **Calculate the average value:**\n   There are 5 numbers in the set, so we divide the sum by 5:\n   \\[\n   \\text{Average} = \\frac{30z}{5} = 6z\n   \\]\n\nFinal answer: \n\\[\n\\boxed{6z}\n\\]",
